---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';

// Each product's own policy covers what that product collects and stores.
const products = [
  { name: 'SSLBoard', href: 'https://sslboard.com/privacy-policy/', site: 'sslboard.com' },
  { name: 'quickS3', href: 'https://quicks3.com/privacy/', site: 'quicks3.com' },
];

const processors = [
  { name: 'Stripe', purpose: 'payments, subscriptions and invoices' },
  { name: 'Cloudflare', purpose: 'hosting, storage, and protection against attacks' },
  { name: 'Postmark', purpose: 'transactional email such as sign-in links and invitations' },
  { name: 'Google', purpose: 'sign-in with Google, where you choose it' },
  { name: 'Ahrefs Analytics', purpose: 'aggregate visit counts on our marketing sites' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Gone Coding Ltd. handles personal data across its products, including SSLBoard and quickS3."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <p class="font-mono text-[13px] text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        This policy covers personal data handled by Gone Coding Ltd. across its products and
        websites. Each product also has its own policy describing what that product stores.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">1. Who is responsible</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Gone Coding Ltd., Unit 1603, The L. Plaza, 367-375 Queen's Road Central, Sheung Wan, Hong
          Kong, is the data controller for the personal data described here. Contact us at
          <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@gone-coding.com">contact@gone-coding.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">2. Product policies</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Our products differ in what they access, so each has its own policy. Read it alongside
          this one:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
          {products.map((product) => (
            <li>
              <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href={product.href}>
                {product.name} privacy policy
              </a>{' '}
              ({product.site})
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">3. What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground">Account data.</span> Your name, email address, and the
            organisation you belong to, plus sign-in records such as when you last signed in.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground">Billing data.</span> Company name, billing address, tax
            ID, and a record of subscriptions and invoices. Card details go directly to Stripe. We
            never see or store a full card number.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground">Product data.</span> What you set up and do inside a
            product, such as the domains you monitor or the storage connections, permissions and
            activity records a product keeps. The product's own policy sets out the detail and how
            long records are kept.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground">Technical data.</span> Server logs, including IP address,
            browser type and timestamps, which we use to run and secure the service.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-foreground">Support messages.</span> What you send us by email.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">4. Why we use it</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
          <li>to provide the product you signed up for, which is the performance of our contract with you</li>
          <li>to take payment and meet accounting and tax obligations, which is a legal obligation</li>
          <li>to keep the service secure, prevent abuse, and fix problems, which is our legitimate interest</li>
          <li>to answer your questions and send service messages such as sign-in links and billing notices</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We do not sell personal data, and we do not use your product data to train AI models.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">5. Who we share it with</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We use a small number of service providers, who process data on our instructions:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
          {processors.map((processor) => (
            <li>
              <span class="text-foreground">{processor.name}</span> for {processor.purpose}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We may also share data where the law requires it, or to establish or defend legal claims.
          If a product is ever sold or transferred, we will tell you before your data moves.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">6. Where data is held</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We are based in Hong Kong, and our providers operate in several countries, so your data
          may be processed outside the place where you are. Where required, we rely on the
          safeguards our providers offer, such as standard contractual clauses. Some products let
          you choose a region for your data; where they do, their own policy explains it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">7. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We keep account and product data while your account is active, and delete or anonymise it
          within a reasonable period after you close it, except where we must keep records longer,
          such as invoices for tax purposes. Individual products apply shorter retention to some
          records, such as activity logs, and say so in their own policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">8. Your rights</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access your personal data, correct
          it, delete it, object to or restrict how we use it, and receive a copy in a portable
          form. Write to
          <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@gone-coding.com"> contact@gone-coding.com</a>
          and we will answer within the time the law allows. You may also complain to your local
          data protection authority.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">9. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Our applications use cookies that are needed to keep you signed in. On our marketing
          sites we use privacy-friendly analytics that count visits without tracking individuals
          across the web. We do not run advertising trackers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">10. Security</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We protect data in transit and at rest, encrypt credentials you entrust to a product, and
          limit access to the few people who need it. No system is perfectly secure, but we will
          tell you without undue delay if a breach affects your personal data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">11. Children</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Our products are for business use and are not directed at children. We do not knowingly
          collect personal data from anyone under 16.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">12. Changes</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We may update this policy. If a change materially affects you, we will tell you by email
          or in the product before it takes effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">13. Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Privacy questions: <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@gone-coding.com">contact@gone-coding.com</a>.
          For a specific product, you can also write to
          <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@sslboard.com">contact@sslboard.com</a>
          or
          <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@quicks3.com">contact@quicks3.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
